Topic 22 – Exception Handling
Objective: try-catch, multiple catch, finally, throw, throws, checked and unchecked exceptions and custom exceptions.
No.	Program	Requirement
01	Arithmetic Exception	Handle division by zero using try-catch.
02	Array Index Exception	Handle accessing an invalid array index.
03	Null Pointer Exception	Create a null String reference and handle the exception when invoking a method.
04	Multiple Catch Blocks	Handle different exceptions using multiple catch blocks.
05	Finally Block	Demonstrate the execution of finally with and without an exception.
06	Throw Keyword	Throw an exception manually when age is below 18.
07	Throws Keyword	Create a method that declares a checked exception using throws. Handle it in the calling method.
08	Custom Exception	Create a custom InvalidLoginException and throw it when login credentials are invalid.
09	Exception Propagation	Create multiple methods where an exception is propagated from one method to another. Handle it at the appropriate level.
10	QA Test Execution Exception	Create a test execution method that throws a custom exception when a test configuration is invalid. Handle the exception in the runner.